WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.665 --> 00:00:02.998
(footsteps)

00:00:06.344 --> 00:00:09.519
(woman groans)

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:10.872
- Good to know you haven't
gotten any stronger

00:00:10.872 --> 00:00:12.901
since we broke up.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.452
That was a weak-ass punch.

00:00:14.452 --> 00:00:17.762
- Yo, Melinda, check this out.

00:00:17.762 --> 00:00:18.762
- Oh my God.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.552
Oh, God, that hurt so bad.

00:00:21.552 --> 00:00:23.064
Why would you throw that at me?

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:25.738
(brass fanfare)

00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:27.988
(gunshots)

00:00:29.441 --> 00:00:31.407
- Why do you think Sahara would

00:00:31.407 --> 00:00:33.014
just trash her room and leave?

00:00:33.014 --> 00:00:33.847
- I don't know.

00:00:33.847 --> 00:00:35.451
I thought that we were getting along.

00:00:35.451 --> 00:00:37.767
Unless she was kidnapped.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:38.812
But who would kidnap her?

00:00:38.812 --> 00:00:40.062
- Who wouldn't?

00:00:41.521 --> 00:00:43.624
I just realized how creepy that sounded

00:00:43.624 --> 00:00:44.766
and I retract that statement.

00:00:44.766 --> 00:00:47.639
- It does appear that there
were signs of a struggle.

00:00:47.639 --> 00:00:50.606
- Wait, can we circle back
to who would kidnap Sahara?

00:00:50.606 --> 00:00:53.340
- I don't know, like North Korea, Russia?

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.989
Whoever kidnaps spies, normally.

00:00:54.989 --> 00:00:56.406
- Sahara's a spy?

00:00:58.108 --> 00:01:00.331
God damn, that's (beep) cool.

00:01:00.331 --> 00:01:01.760
- I gotta stop telling people that.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.123
- Well, if she's kidnapped
then we gotta find her.

00:01:04.123 --> 00:01:06.593
- Or, we could call the police
and they could find her.

00:01:06.593 --> 00:01:07.927
- Or we use Find my iPhone.

00:01:07.927 --> 00:01:08.982
- Or the police.

00:01:08.982 --> 00:01:10.806
- Quit being such a wimp, come on.

00:01:10.806 --> 00:01:12.053
- What, I'm not a wimp.

00:01:12.053 --> 00:01:12.886
You're a wimp.

00:01:12.886 --> 00:01:13.824
- Oh, please.

00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:15.138
Why are you selling your car?

00:01:15.138 --> 00:01:18.293
- There was a spider on my steering wheel.

00:01:18.293 --> 00:01:19.433
I am not a wimp.

00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:21.262
Hack her phone, do it now.

00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:22.115
- Already did.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.063
- Oh, wow.

00:01:23.063 --> 00:01:24.513
Movies don't lie, it
really takes no time at all

00:01:24.513 --> 00:01:25.859
to hack somebody's phone.

00:01:25.859 --> 00:01:27.463
- I know, right, it's crazy.

00:01:27.463 --> 00:01:30.356
Okay, turning on Find My iPhone now.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.910
- Why kidnap me?

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:32.743
- Because you're--

00:01:32.743 --> 00:01:33.880
(cell phone vibrates)

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.737
Are you kidding me?

00:01:34.737 --> 00:01:35.920
No one took her phone.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.151
Susan?

00:01:37.151 --> 00:01:37.984
Vlad?

00:01:39.323 --> 00:01:40.486
You are all useless.

00:01:40.486 --> 00:01:41.702
(phone breaks)

00:01:41.702 --> 00:01:43.452
Especially you, Vlad.

00:01:45.698 --> 00:01:46.865
- I got a hit.

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:50.036
- Let's go.

00:01:51.784 --> 00:01:52.701
- You good?

00:01:54.015 --> 00:01:56.322
- You're just mad I
dumped you, aren't you?

00:01:56.322 --> 00:01:57.822
- Wow, here we go.

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:01.575
Classic Sahara, making
everything about her.

00:02:01.575 --> 00:02:03.360
- Then why am I here, Zoe?

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.008
- Because you're an asset
to the U.S. government

00:02:06.008 --> 00:02:08.388
and that makes you an asset to me.

00:02:08.388 --> 00:02:09.800
- Why?

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.302
What do you want with the government?

00:02:11.302 --> 00:02:13.722
- I'm sorry, do you
think this is Bond film?

00:02:13.722 --> 00:02:15.361
And I'm gonna tell you my evil plan

00:02:15.361 --> 00:02:17.589
in a giant monologue
while your partner bursts

00:02:17.589 --> 00:02:20.006
through the door to save you?

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.008
Goddamnit, Vlad.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:26.222
- I brought lemonade in
case anyone was parched.

00:02:26.222 --> 00:02:28.889
(ominous music)

00:02:30.892 --> 00:02:32.288
- Okay, this is a bad idea.

00:02:32.288 --> 00:02:33.553
I'm definitely calling the cops.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:34.656
- I thought you weren't a wimp.

00:02:34.656 --> 00:02:35.972
- Okay, there's a different
between being brave

00:02:35.972 --> 00:02:37.410
and being stupid.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:38.820
- Not that much of a difference.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:39.987
Leroy Jenkins.

00:02:42.146 --> 00:02:42.979
- Matt?

00:02:42.979 --> 00:02:45.700
- Hey, just coming to save you.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.134
- But, let's hurry up and save
her because I don't know--

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.644
- Let's not and say we did.

00:02:49.644 --> 00:02:50.477
- Jesus, Zoe.

00:02:50.477 --> 00:02:52.478
Did you get your one-liners
from a nineties book of cliches?

00:02:52.478 --> 00:02:53.311
- Shut up.

00:02:53.311 --> 00:02:55.880
Come any closer and I'll
slice this dorky girl's neck.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.213
- Slice my neck?

00:03:00.021 --> 00:03:02.104
- Wow, that is one weak--

00:03:11.118 --> 00:03:13.470
(police sirens blare)

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.407
- Okay, they said we're free to go.

00:03:15.407 --> 00:03:17.937
- Good, I just want to go
home and lay on the couch

00:03:17.937 --> 00:03:19.440
and never leave the house again

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.376
but I guess that makes me a wimp.

00:03:21.376 --> 00:03:22.419
- Are you kidding?

00:03:22.419 --> 00:03:24.584
Your wimpiness saved us.

00:03:24.584 --> 00:03:26.622
When you passed out and
collapsed in her arms,

00:03:26.622 --> 00:03:28.175
it left her confused and vulnerable

00:03:28.175 --> 00:03:29.635
so that I could deliver the final blow.

00:03:29.635 --> 00:03:30.799
- Like a boss.

00:03:30.799 --> 00:03:31.995
- [Sahara] We definitely tag-teamed her.

00:03:31.995 --> 00:03:33.150
- We did?

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.750
- You killed it, dude.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:35.868
- I'm a wimp?

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:37.811
- Oh, yeah, the wimpiest.

00:03:37.811 --> 00:03:38.862
- I'm a wimp.

00:03:38.862 --> 00:03:40.074
- Okay, stop yelling.

00:03:40.074 --> 00:03:41.468
- Yes, let's get an ice cream.

00:03:41.468 --> 00:03:42.301
Who wants an ice cream?

00:03:42.301 --> 00:03:43.625
- I'm so hungry, yes.

00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:46.458
(exciting music)

